(10-40 psia); vaporizing and flashing said entrained liquid from said low pressure flash zone to produce a predominantly isobutane low pressure flash zone flash stream; compressing and cooling said low pressure flash zone flash stream to produce a compressed low pressure flash zone flash stream and combining said compressed low pressure flash zone flash stream with said high pressure flash gas stream to give a total recycle isobutane stream; dividing said total recycle isobutane stream into two streams, a main isobutane recycle stream which comprises 88-92 per cent of said isobutane in said total recycle isobutane stream, and an isobutane recycle slip stream which comprises the remainder of said isobutane in said total recycle isobutane stream; passing said main isobutane recycle stream through a treating zone to remove water and then to said polymerization zone; 

 passing said isobutane recycle slip stream along with fresh 1-hexene feed through a first fractionation zone to separate out essentially all of said 1-hexene contained in said isobutane recycle slip stream and recovering an essentially 1- hexene-free isobutane recycle slip stream; passing said essentially 1-hexene-free isobutane recycle slip stream to a second fractionation zone where lights including ethylene are removed to give and essentially olefin-free isobutane recycle slip stream; cooling said essentially olefin-free isobutane recycle slip stream to give a cooled essentially olefin-free isobutane recycle slip stream; passing said cooled essentially olefin-free isobutane recycle slip stream to a catalyst mixing zone where it is used to produce a catalyst mud comprising chromium oxide on silica; and passing said catalyst mud to said polymerization zone. 17. A process comprising: copolymerizing ethylene and a higher 1 -olefin in a polymerization zone in the presence of a liquid diluent to produce a copolymer; withdrawing an effluent from said polymerization zone, said effluent comprising withdrawn solid copolymer, withdrawn diluent, withdrawn unreacted ethylene and withdrawn unreacted higher 1 -olefin; passing said effluent into a flash zone under conditions of temperature and pressure such that a major portion of fluid components therein flash overhead to form a flash gas stream; recovering said withdrawn solid copolymer and remaining fluid components from said flash zone as a product of said process; dividing said flash gas stream into two streams, a main withdrawn diluent recycle stream which constitutes a major portion of said flash gas stream, and a withdrawn diluent recycle slip stream which constitutes a minor portion of said flash gas stream; recycling said main withdrawn diluent recycle stream to said polymerization zone; passing said withdrawn diluent recycle slip stream and a fresh higher 1 -olefin feed to a higher 1 -olefin degassing zone; 

 withdrawing from said higher 1 -olefin degassing zone a degassed higher 1 -olefin comonomer feed stream and an overhead stream comprising diluent and ethylene; passing said overhead stream comprising diluent and ethylene to a lights removal zone; removing ethylene as an overhead stream from said lights removal zone and recovering an at least essentially olefin-free diluent recycle stream as a product of said lights removal zone; and passing said at least essentially olefm-free diluent recycle slip stream to a catalyst mixing zone.

19. Apparatus comprising in combination: a closed loop reactor having a continuous take off means for recovering reactor effluent; a high pressure flash tank having a high pressure vapor flash take off means in an upper portion thereof and a polymer take off means in a lower portion thereof; a heated flash line connecting said continuous take off means with said high pressure flash tank to convey said effluent to said high pressure flash tank; a liquid-vapor separation vessel having an inlet, a vapor flash take off means in an upper portion thereof and a liquid take off means in a lower portion thereof; a first conduit connecting said vapor flash take off means of said high pressure flash tank and said inlet of said liquid-vapor separation vessel to convey overhead from said high pressure flash tank to said liquid-vapor separation vessel; a heavies removal column having an inlet means, an overhead vapor recovery means, an intermediate product take off means and a lower heavies removal means; at least one second conduit means connecting said first conduit and said heavies removal column inlet means for taking a slip stream off from said first conduit; 

 a third conduit means connecting said vapor flash take off means of said vapor-liquid separation vessel and said at least one second conduit means; a fourth conduit means connecting said liquid take off means of said liquid-vapor separation vessel and said closed loop reactor; a diluent degassing column having an inlet, overhead means to remove vapor and a lower product recovery means; a fifth conduit means connecting said overhead vapor recovery means of said heavies removal column and said inlet of said diluent degassing column a mud drum for mixing catalyst and diluent; a sixth conduit means connecting said lower product recovery means of said diluent degassing column and said mud drum for passing degassed product from said diluent degassing column to said mud drum; a seventh conduit connecting said mud drum and said closed loop reactor means for passing catalyst mud to said closed loop reactor means; an eighth conduit means for introducing comonomer to said heavies removal column; a ninth conduit for introducing diluent in open communication with said fifth conduit; a tenth conduit for introducing monomer, said tenth conduit being in open communication with said fourth conduit; and conduit means connected to said mud drum for introducing catalyst into said mud drum. 20. Apparatus in accordance with claim 19 comprising in addition: a low pressure flash tank having an inlet, an overhead vapor outlet and a lower polymer recovery outlet; conduit means connecting said polymer take off means of said high pressure flash tank and said inlet of said low pressure flash tank; vapor compression means having an inlet means and an outlet means; conduit means connecting said overhead vapor outlet of said low pressure flash tank and said inlet means of said compression means for conveying fluid from said low pressure flash tank to said compression means; and 

 conduit means connecting said outlet means of said compression means and said first conduit to convey compressed fluid to said first conduit.
